mothershipOS (mship.video): the encoder takes frames that are virtio-gpu buffers in its layout as they are (DMABUF
input). Before the input queue streams, the first frame decides its memory: one in Venus's layout (single-planar
NV12, the device's strides and chroma offset; a mothershipOS host's NV12 gralloc buffers, e.g. the camera's video
buffers) that is a virtio-gpu buffer (fdinfo exp_name) goes to the host's Venus where it is; other frames keep the
MMAP copy of patch 0010. The bitstream stays MMAP.

